Why would you need tins of nymph? Tengus can also give you teleportitis. 
The chance for getting teleportitis from a tengu is actually higher than 
the chance for getting teleport control. (I think that is the reason why 
it is a good idea to tin many of them and eat all the tins at once 
instead of eating each of them fresh).

In my last game I ate a tengu (fresh, not tinned) in the hope of getting 
teleport control. It gave me teleportitis instead. But I was lucky and 
had a ring of teleport control. I only got intrinsic teleport control 
when my wizard reached level 17.

If I remember correctly, one nymph or leprechaun is enough for getting 
teleportitis.


